  "body": "**Research note: a proved scheduling bound and a priced negative result. No \u03ba claim; the selected record and `upstream/` are unchanged.** Only `research/multipair-schedule-bound/` is added.\n\nTwo B_K conventions have never been varied: one bank pair per local-word invocation (format-limits-corrected rule-table row 13) and the pairwise exchange \u03c1 (row 5). The format-limits ceiling theorem explicitly does not cover non-B_K schedules. This package closes that gap.\n\n- **Theorem S (written proof, checked).** Any schedule of shear-type local words with `s` stages over `K` bank pairs needs `N \u2265 2K + \u23082K/(s\u22121)\u2309` local-word invocations. This holds for any number of pairs per stage, mixed orientations, arbitrary block-diagonal bridges, any pair-level signed \u03c1 and port-level calls. It generalises `research/cross-shear-stage-bound`.\n- **Consequence.** Per port, `D/W \u2264 1 \u2212 (cst/v)\u00b7s/(s\u22121)`, so every schedule is dominated port for port by the B-template at the same `s`. The proof tracks row-space intersections with `X` and `Y` and charges each stage's rank to progress or \"waste\".\n- **Attainment.** At odd `s`, parallel borrowing chains attain the bound. Seven schedules replay exactly to the signed exchange, including rank-2v stages that mix forward and backward words. `B_4` reproduces the (Sch) idle windows.\n- **Even s.** Exhaustive GF(2) searches give the K = 2 frontier exactly equal to the bound. At (K = 3, s = 4), the smallest even case, the bound is **not** attained: an unrestricted equality search over all 2,051 stage shapes finds no schedule.\n- **Priced on PR #1800's T74 words.** The best attained schedule reproduces the T74 complex exponent `0.001679754956125544521335` exactly and does not beat it. s = 7 hits the hosting wall; s = 11/13/15 lose 1.40/3.71/6.46% of b. The only open point, s = 8 if the bound were attained there, is worth at most +0.26% (window-aligned idle) or +0.70% (packing ceiling).\n- **Multi-pair invocations share nothing.** Pairs active in the same stage carry independent data, so each keeps its own centre path and helper network (Lemma Q excludes the fused unit). This differs from the temporal centre-sharing PRs #1708/#1748/#1791/#1829/#1838.\n\n### Reproduce\n\n```sh\npython3 -B research/multipair-schedule-bound/verify.py\npython3.12 scripts/research_package.py --package research/multipair-schedule-bound\n```\n\nExpected final markers: `PASS_MULTIPAIR_SCHEDULE_BOUND` and `PASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE ... outcome=negative-result`. The verifier takes about 30 s and uses the standard library only. Both pass locally on Windows with CPython 3.11 and 3.12. Hosted CI is not claimed.\n\nThe verifier checks:\n- the proof-step inequalities on 10,697 random stages over GF(2), GF(3) and GF(5), with two false-strengthening controls that must fail;\n- the exact chain replays, byte-equal to the committed output;\n- the exhaustive K = 2 frontier;\n- recomputed exact prices for 14 schedule families, using the retained moment engine and `complex-local-word-ceiling/ceiling.py`.\n\nThree negative controls must be rejected: a flipped chain sign, a perturbed T74 extract, and a below-bound schedule. The longer K = 3 searches have committed outputs and commands in the README; they are not rerun by `verify.py`.\n\n### Scope and inputs\n\n- `inputs/T74-WORDS.json` is an extract of PR #1800's provider registry, with its source commit, Git blob and SHA256 pinned. It holds the two local words' per-call profiles, helper widths and call split. The verifier recomposes PR #1800's published global profile from it exactly. The T74 construction itself is **not** re-verified here.\n- Not covered:\n  - even-`s` attainment beyond (K = 3, s = 4);\n  - \u03c1 through a third bank class (the \"two unpaid coordinates\" lever);\n  - non-shear local words;\n  - a frame-checker replay of mixed-orientation stages (legality is argued from the contract).\n- Card `coverage-law-change`, scope **changed**: this tests the schedule freedom, not two unpaid coordinates. TASK.json records the reason and two structured open questions.\n- Overlap: `find_overlap.py` was refreshed before submission. Nothing on record covers multi-pair or mixed-orientation schedules.\n\n### Credit\n\nThe work builds on:\n- `cross-shear-stage-bound` and the archived borrowing-chain campaign;\n- `format-limits-corrected` (rule table, (Sch)/(Dfc), Lemma Q);\n- `complex-local-word-ceiling`;\n- PR #1800 (jeremykothe2) and its T74 lineage (PR1625 mdumitrean, PR1661 midhatn, PR1319/PR1297 rohanarun and others) for the priced words.\n\nPrepared by themilkman216 with substantial Claude (Anthropic) assistance; the investigation ran as parallel fresh-context research branches. Apache-2.0. No independent human review is claimed.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
